  "worked_solution": "Let's simplify the expression using the properties of logical operation\n\n- First, we use a De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n\u00ac[\u00acA\u2228(A\u2227\u00acB)]\u2261\u00ac\u00acA\u2227\u00ac(A\u2227\u00acB)\n$$\n\n- Next, we simplify the double negation:\n\n$$\n\u00ac\u00acA\u2227\u00ac(A\u2227\u00acB)\u2261A\u2227\u00ac(A\u2227\u00acB)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use a De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\nA\u2227\u00ac(A\u2227\u00acB)\u2261A\u2227(\u00acA\u2228\u00ac\u00acB)\n$$\n\n- Next, we simplify the double negation:\n\n$$\nA\u2227(\u00acA\u2228\u00ac\u00acB)\u2261A\u2227(\u00acA\u2228B)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use the distributive law (conjunction over disjunction):\n\n$$\nA\u2227(\u00acA\u2228B)\u2261(A\u2227\u00acA)\u2228(A\u2227B)\n$$\n\n- Next, we use the fact that the conjunction of a statement and its negation is a contradiction:\n\n$$\n(A\u2227\u00acA)\u2228(A\u2227B)\u2261c\u2228(A\u2227B)\n$$\n\n- Finally, we use the fact that the disjunction of a statement and a contradiction equals the original statement:\n\n$$\nc\u2228(A\u2227B)\u2261A\u2227B\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\u00ac[\u00acA\u2228(A\u2227\u00acB)]\u2261A\u2227B.\n$$",
